      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="msv__faq">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do I lose CPP/OAS if I move to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">No. Canada allows you to receive CPP and OAS abroad indefinitely. However, you must file Canadian taxes on this income and comply with CRA (Canada Revenue Agency) requirements. OAS is subject to repayment if your income exceeds the threshold (~$90k CAD for 2026).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What is the Canada-Spain Tax Treaty?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">The Canada-Spain Tax Treaty prevents double taxation on the same income. It specifies which country taxes different types of income (pensions, investment income, rental income, etc.). Understanding this treaty is essential to minimize your overall tax burden.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do I need to file Canadian taxes if I move to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Yes, if you have Canadian-source income (CPP, pensions, investments, rental property). You must file Canadian taxes as long as you have Canadian connections. You also file Spanish taxes if you're tax resident in Spain (>183 days). The treaty prevents double taxation on the same income.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What happens to my RRSP when I move abroad?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Your RRSP doesn't automatically change. However, withdrawals are fully taxable in Canada and Spain. You can leave it invested in Canada. The treaty generally allows Canada to tax RRSP withdrawals. Consider your withdrawal strategy before moving.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Is my TFSA affected if I move to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">You can still contribute to and hold a TFSA, but growth and withdrawals lose their tax-free status in Spain. Spain taxes investment growth. You still can't withdraw penalty-free for Canadian purposes. The account structure becomes complicated if you're tax resident in Spain.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ How do I notify the CRA I'm moving?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Use Form NR73 (Departure from Canada) if leaving Canada. File it with CRA. You must file a final Canadian tax return for the year of departure. After that, file Canadian taxes annually if you have Canadian-source income. Keep CRA informed of your address (even if in Spain).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
